# LongRoad.Core & LongRoad

## Core (base systems — including shared game systems)

- Reusable building blocks: scriptable/entity bases, shared entities (`Person`, traits, statuses), `GameEventBase`, localization, input wrappers, `LongRoadBehaviourCore`.
- May contain **shared game logic** (e.g. person heal/hunger/status helpers) when it is a base used by many features.
- May use Unity APIs and Packages (NaughtyAttributes, DOTween, Localization).
- Prefer Domain for pure algorithms that do not need Unity types.
- Do **not** put the main turn/scene pipeline, screens, or one-off feature scripts here — that is LongRoad.

## LongRoad (main pipeline, UI, features)

- Composes Domain + Core into the playable game.
- **Naming**: `*Manager` = `MonoBehaviour` controllers (prefer `LongRoadBehaviour`); `*Service` = plain classes implementing `IService`, placed in `Services/` (`LongRoad.Services`). Inject service dependencies via **constructor**, not `Init(...)`. Exception: `GamePipeline` (full turn loop) stays at assembly root, no `Service` suffix.
- **`GameManager`**: global singleton (`DontDestroyOnLoad`) for shared services (input, localization).
- **`LocalManager`**: owns `GameData` (store only), `GamePipeline`, `PersonService`, `InventoryService`, `GameTimeService`, `TravelService`, `LocationService`, `MoneyService`; calls `CarModelManager.Init` / `GameUIManager.Init` after services are ready.
- **`GameUIManager`**: scene UI host (`UIDocument` + MainUI); caches slots (`Hud`, `Content`, `Party`, `Inventory`, `Location`, `Overlay`); initializes registered `GameUIElement` children. Access via `Local.UI`.
- **`CarModelManager`**: spawns `CarModel`; `SetState` / `RefreshState` from pipeline/travel/fuel events (services do not know about managers).
- **`HudStatusUI`**: HUD turn/day/period + Continue («Поехали»).
- **`GameData`**: session fields only (Car, Turn, Day, IsDaytime, Money, TravelledKm, CurrentLocation, Route) — no events/logic.
- **`GameTimeService`**: turn advance after phase 3; day/night every 3 turns; UI events `OnTurnChanged` / `OnDayNightChanged` / `OnDayChanged`.
- **`TravelService`**: road progress (`DistancePerTurn` km) when not at a location; arrive on absolute route distance. UI: `OnTravelProgress` / `OnArrived` / `OnDeparted`.
- **`LocationService`**: gas/shop/hospital/entertainment/leave at `CurrentLocation`. UI: `OnChanged`.
- **`MoneyService`**: `TrySpend` / `Add` on `GameData.Money`. UI: `OnMoneyChanged`.
- **`GamePipeline`**: (1) player, (2) modifiers + bound Status/Trait, (3) random `[UseGameEvent]`, then `AdvanceTurn` + `AdvanceTravel`. UI: `OnPhaseChanged`, `OnEnded`.
- **`PersonService`** (`IService`): party; phase-2 tick. UI: `OnPersonAdded` / `OnPersonRemoved` / `OnModifiersApplied`.
- **`InventoryService`** (`IService`): cargo; `UseItem` + bound Item events. UI: `OnChanged` / item add/remove/used.
- Prefer subclassing `LongRoadBehaviour` for access to `Game` / `Local` / `UI`.
- Concrete events subclass `GameEventBase`. Use `[UseGameEvent]` for phase-3; `[BoundGameEvent(kind, tag)]` for Status/Trait/Item. Catalogs cached.
- UI subscribes to services / pipeline / entities — not `GameData`. Slot VisualElements come only from `GameUIManager`.
- UI and feature systems call into Core/Domain bases; avoid reinventing shared entity rules in UI callbacks.
- Keep MonoBehaviours thin: orchestrate, don’t bury reusable rules only usable from one screen.

## Content & localization

- Place game assets under `Assets/_Game/Resources/` (characters, cars, items, locations, routes, specialities, traits, locales, scenes).
- Entity strings: `{Tag}_name`, `{Tag}_desc` (Entities table). UI strings: Main table.
- Locales: `en-US`, `ru-RU`.
- Inventory: global `InventoryService`; stacks by `Item.Tag`; weight limited by selected `Car.MaxWeight`.
- Travel: `Route` stops with absolute `DistanceFromStartKm`; `Car.DistancePerTurn` km per road turn.

## Motion

- Use **DOTween** for simple animations (UI fades/moves, short feedback tweens).

## Both

- Root namespaces: `LongRoad.Core` / `LongRoad`.
- Do not reference Editor-only APIs from runtime assemblies.
